{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_09e005ef3b60209dc048841d3f88e6f072aad36e41f763aa909adcf3590807be", "title": "Louise of Sweden", "text": "Louise of Sweden (Louise Josephine Eugenie (Swedish: \"Lovisa Josefina Eugenia\" ); 31 October 1851 – 20 March 1926), was Queen of Denmark as the spouse of King Frederick VIII. She was the only surviving child of Charles XV of Sweden and his consort, Louise of the Netherlands.", "score": 25.9734}, {"id": "hp_doc_37bbe1204ea641faba14b07db63efd670cd3cc4f0feec6a1631277e7c049f9db", "title": "John Motley Morehead III", "text": "John Motley Morehead III (November 3, 1870 – January 7, 1965) was a chemist whose work provided much of the foundation for the business of Union Carbide Corporation. He was a noted philanthropist who made major gifts to his alma mater, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill. He also served as mayor of Rye, New York and United States Ambassador to Sweden. His father was James Turner Morehead; his grandfather John Motley Morehead served as Governor of North Carolina. His sister Lily Morehead Mebane was decorated by the governments of France and Serbia for her relief work after World War I; she later served two terms in the North Carolina state legislature.", "score": 11.5724}, {"id": "hp_doc_b178744283316d154a4a86b205747a269a1fabab31d74c43e10c32dc2abe2207", "title": "Father of the Bride Part II", "text": "Father of the Bride Part II is a 1995 American comedy film starring Steve Martin, Diane Keaton and Martin Short. It is a sequel to \"Father of the Bride\" and a loose remake of the 1951 film \"Father's Little Dividend\", the sequel to the original \"Father of the Bride\" film released in 1950.", "score": 11.403}], "remaining_searches": 1}
